wallpaper-manager (2.0.9.0-0~ubuntu26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium
  * A minor bug was fixed; the CONFIG_FONT file (containing the "selected font") is ignored if set to `false`, so `FONTE_DEFAULT` is not used, on wallpaper-con-citas (1.2.2).
  * 1.2.1 Error fixed: the translation file that had been lost was recovered. 
  * Up to date on wallpaper-con-citas (1.2.0). The language flag—which allows switching between English and Spanish—now also supports: Arabic, Bengali, German, Greek, Persian (Iran), French, Gujarati, Hindi, Indonesian, Italian, Japanese, Lithuanian, Portuguese, Romanian, Russian, Slovak, Tamil, Thai, Ukrainian, Simplified Chinese, and Traditional Chinese.
  * ☝️ These languages ​​are available on the Sadhguru and Prem Rawat websites.
  * For Siva P. and Sri Sri Ravi Shankar—as well as the "Other authors"—we use the `translate` command.
  * It also remembers the selected language upon restarting.
  * The font selector now includes thumbnails showing the font icon, providing a visual reference for the typeface's style. You can also configure it to remember your chosen font upon restarting, or it will default to: `./fonts/C059-BdIta.t1`. Hope you enjoy it.

